  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>If the potential difference between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi></math> is zero, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>.&nbsp;The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> is ______.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/fdcbe7f9-686f-4a25-bb20-4085d35f9a69-9895901.PNG\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 249px;\" />&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/fdcbe7f9-686f-4a25-bb20-4085d35f9a69-9895901.PNG\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 249px;\" /></p><p>As potential difference between B &amp; D is zero therefore it is&nbsp;a balanced&nbsp;wheatstone bridge. So, we can write</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, required&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p>",
